>I would appreciate it if someone would tell me what all the suffix options
>with nethack are and what they do.
>
From the manpages of 3.1.3 on my unix system:
   nethack [ -d directory ] [ -n ] [ -[ABCEHKPRSTVW@] ] [ -[DX] ]
           [ -u playername ] [ -dec ] [ -ibm ]

the -n option suppresses printing of any news from the game administrator
the -[ABCEHKPRSTVW@] determines the character role. a -@ gives you
     a random role.
the -D or -X option will start the game in  a  special  non-
     scoring  discovery mode.  -D will, if the player is the game
     administrator, start in debugging (wizard) mode instead.
the -dec/ibm defines what kind of display you want (I guess... never used it)


>On the net I have heard mention of a wizard mode. What is that, and what can it
>do?

You access wizard/discovery mode as explained above, and discovery mode can
also be accessed from within the game via the 'X' command (It will turn your
current game into discovery mode)

In discovery mode, you can continue playing even if you die (You are prompted
a choice). There is no way to go from discovery to normal mode, so once you
decide to enter it, there is no return.

Wizard mode can only be accessed via the -D command line option, and it is
much like discovery mode, except you have some extra powers, like auto-
identify, unlimited wishes, and some other powers. All these are listed in
the online help ('?')

